{
    "en":
    {
        "NT_EXPANSION_NAME": "Nautilus",
        "NT_EXPANSION_DESC": "Adds content from 'Nautilus' to the game.",

        "NT_INTERACTABLE_SHRINEOFTHEDEEP_NAME": "Shrine of the Deep",
        "NT_INTERACTABLE_SHRINEOFTHEDEEP_CONTEXT": "<style=cIsVoid>Challenge the Void</style>",
        "NT_INTERACTABLE_SHRINEOFTHEDEEP_DESCRIPTION": "Interact to <style=cIsVoid>challenge the Void</style>, increasing teleporter boss difficulty and spawning <style=cIsVoid>Voidtouched</style> enemies. In exchange, all dropped <style=cShrine>boss items</style> will be converted into <style=cIsVoid>void boss items</style>.",
        "NT_INTERACTABLE_SHRINEOFTHEDEEP_MESSAGE": "<style=cIsVoid>You call out to the Void...</style>",

        "NT_ITEM_WELLIES_NAME": "Waterlogged Wellies",
        "NT_ITEM_WELLIES_PICKUP": "On hit, weaken airborne enemies and pull them to the ground. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Hiker's Boots.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_WELLIES_DESC": "Hitting an airborne enemy pulls them downward <style=cStack>(with additional strength per stack)</style>, and <style=cIsDamage>Weakens</style> them for <style=cIsDamage>{0}</style> seconds <style=cStack>(+{1} seconds per stack)</style>, <style=cIsDamage>reducing their armor by 30 and their movement speed and damage by 40%.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Hiker's Boots.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_WELLIES_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Audio recording transcript ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘helmet found near outside large void anomaly. boot nearby but i didn’t want to touch it’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘poor guy’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>UES-1 = Commando designation employee ‘Lance Bernard’, last seen aboard UES Contact Light prior to disaster. MIA</style>\n<style=cStack>UES-2 = Unknown UES employee, assumed MIA</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nUES-1 : Hey, man.\n\nUES-2 : Yeah?\n\nUES-1 : <style=cSub>[mumbling]</style>\n\nUES-2 : What’s good?\n\nUES-1 : Do you know what trench foot is?\n\nUES-2 : Oh.\n\nUES-1 : Yeah. <style=cSub>[grunting]</style>\n\nUES-2 : Do you want to stop?\n\nUES-1 : Nah, I just. <style=cSub>[long pause]</style> I hoped you had a cure or something to help, or something. It doesn’t hurt, but I don’t think I should keep walking on it.\n\nUES-2 : No. I don’t know, maybe. Can I take a look?\n\n<style=cSub>[they seem to stop and find a spot to rest]</style>\n\n<style=cSub>[high pitched sound, presumed whale call (?)]</style>\n\nUES-1 : <style=cSub>[exerting]</style>\n\nUES-2 : Can I?\n\nUES-1 : No, I’ll do it. It doesn’t hurt.\n\n<style=cSub>[wet dropping sound, presumed remains of UES-1’s foot]</style>\n\nUES-2 : Oh, god.\n\nUES-1 : Is that my (?)\n\n<style=cSub>[both retching]</style>\n\nUES-2 : <style=cSub>[expletive]</style>\n\n<style=cSub>[whale call (?)]</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_CRABSINTHE_NAME": "Crabsinthe",
        "NT_ITEM_CRABSINTHE_PICKUP": "Increase passive health regeneration. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Power Elixirs and Empty Bottles.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_CRABSINTHE_DESC": "Increase passive health regeneration by <style=cIsHealing>{0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Power Elixirs{2}.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_CRABSINTHE_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘My field office, Safe Travels drop zone Alpha-2’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Used to be a 1978 vintage Absinthe. It didn’t look like this before.’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Jade S.</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin summary ></style>\n\nThis specimen, originally a bottle of absinthe, has undergone a similar void conversion process to others we’ve studied, but with some unique results.\n\nThe most notable anomaly with this bottle is that it never seems to run out of liquid. I’ve discovered the signature of a miniature wormhole on the bottle’s inner bottom surface (similar to other ‘void portals’ found before), which explains this oddity but doesn’t give me any clue as to where the liquid comes from. Tests with extended draining suggest that there’s a significant wellspring of the liquid somewhere unknown to us.\n\nToxicology analysis has reported this as safe to drink, though it has a similar alcohol content to the original absinthe and should be consumed in moderation. Experimentation has revealed that it tastes fruity and has a viscous texture, like some kind of alcoholic blackberry jam. Further experimentation required.\n\nThe writing on the label is completely different, having been converted into the same glyphics that other labs were reporting with their void specimens-- for lack of a better term, we coined it ‘Crab language’. Thanks to your help with recalling the original text, if the linguists manage to crack the language, we’ll know for sure whether meaning is preserved through conversion.\n\nI don’t know why you seemed so disappointed when you handed this over to me, Captain. This stuff is great!\n\n<style=cStack>< End summary ></style>",
    
        "NT_ITEM_VOIDWATCH_NAME": "Collector's Appraisal",
        "NT_ITEM_VOIDWATCH_PICKUP": "While out of {0}, accumulate a stacking damage buff for your next hit. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Delicate Watches.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_VOIDWATCH_DESC": "While out of {3}, accumulate a <style=cIsDamage>stacking buff</style> every second which increases your <style=cIsDamage>next hit's damage by {0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style>. <style=cIsDamage>Can store up to {2}x{0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{2}x{1}% per stack)</style> <style=cIsDamage>extra damage.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Delicate Watches.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_VOIDWATCH_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Right outside!’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Pre-analytics summary: Jade S.</style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin summary ></style> \n\nI’m not in the field often. I was nervous to go out (we’ve had golem problems lately...), so you can imagine how delighted I was to find a specimen right outside the lab’s front door! \n\nIt’s some kind of mechanical watch. Completely brittle to the touch, having been worn and rusted for what might be millennia. It shattered when I touched it, so please handle with care. \n\nStranger still, it was laid on top of a clipboard covered with writing in unintelligible glyphs. I don’t really know what they say, although… don’t take this as a scientific analysis, but I can FEEL the meaning of the glyphs when I stare at them long enough. This one says something like: \n\n“Faulty mechanism. Return to sender!” \n\n<style=cStack>< End summary ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_VISCOUSPOT_NAME": "Viscous Pot",
        "NT_ITEM_VISCOUSPOT_PICKUP": "Reduce barrier decay, and steal barrier from nearby enemies on secondary skill use. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Luminous Shots.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_VISCOUSPOT_DESC": "<style=cIsHealing>Reduces barrier decay by {0}%.</style> Using your secondary skill launches up to <style=cIsDamage>{1}</style> <style=cStack>(+{2} per stack)</style> <style=cIsDamage>viscous orbs</style> at enemies within <style=cisUtility>{3}m</style> <style=cStack>(+{4}m per stack)</style>, dealing <style=cIsDamage>{5}%</style> damage and granting you <style=cIsHealing>{6}</style> temporary barrier on hit. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Luminous Shots.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_VISCOUSPOT_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Taken from cradle inside void seed’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Please report any sightings to the Captain right away!!!’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Jade S. </style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nI was going to continue the lab analysis, but the potted specimen is missing. I left it for exactly 10 and a half minutes and the thing somehow escaped its container (without breaking the seal, I might add!!) \n\nI suspected the viscous goop inside it was a living organism, but not that it was intelligent enough to leave the lab with no trace. Worse is that I never confirmed whether it was capable of harming humans or not. I’m going to be checking under tables and beds for the next few hours… \n\nAnd before you tell me I should’ve been watching- what could I have done? What do you want to do, ban the science team from taking bathroom breaks?! \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_PALESTAR_NAME": "Pale Star",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTAR_PICKUP": "Convert a chest drop into a Void Potential, and recharge with a Void Cradle. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Sale Stars.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTAR_DESC": "Opening a chest consumes all stacks of this item and converts the chest's reward into a <style=cIsVoid>Void Potential</style> of equivalent rarity, offering a choice between <style=cIsVoid>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> <style=cIsVoid>void items</style>. <style=cisUtility>All stacks of this item regenerate after a Void Cradle is used.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Sale Stars.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTAR_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Stuck to carapace of Reaver corpse’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Store in grav isolation chamber if possible’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Pre-analytics summary: Harvey D.</style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin summary ></style> \n\nThose crabs are smarter than they seem. They’re making new tools out of our salvage-- one nearly blew a hole in my skull with what looked like a carcinized missile launcher. I was able to take the thing down after a careful ambush, and now I’m bringing back the launcher, plus an extra prize I found hanging from its leg: A starfish straight from the Void. \n\nThe first thing this creature did when I picked it up was teleport right onto my weapon and start eating at the barrel! I was about to swat it when I realized that it was spitting up new material in place of what it was consuming- purple, crusty material- until the gun started to look like an entirely new piece of hardware. \n\nWell, I let my curiosity get the best of me, and now I have no weapon. The starfish is no talented gunsmith. It’ll be a tough journey back, but certainly worth it if I’ve found a lead on the source of all these corrupted specimens! \n\nAnd, as I’m writing this, I realize the glove on my suit is starting to crust over and turn into a set of claws... \n\nThe science team will love this one. \n\n<style=cStack>< End summary ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_PALESTARCONSUMED_NAME": "Drained Star",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTARCONSUMED_PICKUP": "Needs to be recharged at a <style=cIsVoid>Void Cradle</style>.",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTARCONSUMED_DESC": "Needs to be recharged at a <style=cIsVoid>Void Cradle</style>.",
        "NT_ITEM_PALESTARCONSUMED_LORE": "<style=cStack>No data...</style>",

        "NT_ITEM_HYDRATOOTH_NAME": "Tooth of Hydra",
        "NT_ITEM_HYDRATOOTH_PICKUP": "Collapse now culminates in a stunning explosion. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Noxious Thorns.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_HYDRATOOTH_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsDamage>{0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style> chance to inflict <style=cIsDamage>collapse</style> on hit. On activation, collapse now creates a <style=cIsDamage>stunning explosion</style> which deals <style=cIsDamage>{2}% damage per stack of collapse</style> to enemies within <style=cIsDamage>{3}m</style> <style=cStack>(+{4}m per stack)</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Noxious Thorns.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_HYDRATOOTH_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Internal UES message thread ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘2058/11/03’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>jadesly123 = Jade S. (UES Safe Travels, Science team apprentice)</style> \n<style=cStack>Mira Li = Mira L. (UES Safe Travels, Science team lead)</style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\njadesly123 <style=cStack>(2058/11/03 11:56)</style> : lunch? \n\njadesly123 <style=cStack>(2058/11/03 17:01)</style> : I found the potted specimen and have returned it to the lab, its now in a fully blink sealed container (magnumite as you suggested), apologies for any problems I might have caused there!! \n\njadesly123 <style=cStack>(2058/11/03 21:10)</style> : Hey, can I log a few extra overtime hours? Ive been really into keeping track of the time on this watch, it looks random but i think the hands go in a pattern. Want to see it? \n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/03 21:32)</style> : [read] \n\njadesly123 <style=cStack>(2058/11/03 21:58)</style> : Sorry are you busy? ill message later :P btw are hydras real or is Harvey telling jokes? he said you’d know \n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/04 01:20)</style> : [read] \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_SHIMMERINGNAUTILUS_NAME": "Shimmering Nautilus",
        "NT_ITEM_SHIMMERINGNAUTILUS_PICKUP": "Resist and retaliate against repeated strikes. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Shattering Justices.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SHIMMERINGNAUTILUS_DESC": "<style=cIsHealing>Reduce all incoming damage by {0}%.</style> After hitting you {1} times, your attacker evokes an orb that strikes them for <style=cIsDamage>{2}% damage</style> <style=cStack>(+{3}% per stack)</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Shattering Justices.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SHIMMERINGNAUTILUS_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Unexplored temple ruins, roughly 21 miles south of drop zone Alpha 2’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘HANDLE CAREFULLY!!!’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Pre-analytics summary: Harvey D.</style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin summary ></style> \n\nWhen I found this little sea shell, I was surprised to find a note, in English, written on a purple sticky note beside it: \n\n“What worries you? No matter. Tap this shell five times for good luck!” \n\nI was not surprised, more so disturbed to find the splattered corpse of one of our commandos surrounding it- at least what remained after the beetles had their fill. I can’t even tell who it was-- maybe Jordan? \n\nI was wise not to heed the instructions, and I instead inspected the material with a field spectrometer. Extremely unstable magnumite, ready to burst at the slightest pressure applied. \n\nSet aside all this void stuff... why? Who would play such a cruel prank? \n\nWhich one of our friends fell for it? \n\n<style=cStack>< End summary ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_MOTHEROFPEARL_NAME": "Mother of Pearl",
        "NT_ITEM_MOTHEROFPEARL_PICKUP": "Collecting a gold chunk fires a volley of missiles. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all War Bonds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_MOTHEROFPEARL_DESC": "Collecting a chunk of gold launches <style=cIsDamage>{0} missiles</style> dealing <style=cIsDamage>{1}% damage</style> <style=cStack>(+{2}% per stack)</style> each. <style=cShrine>Has a flat {3}% chance to convert any pickup into a chunk of gold.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all War Bonds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_MOTHEROFPEARL_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Signal transcript ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Source from: ‘unknown’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\n211405 \n\n211405 \n\n211405 \n\napparatus \n\ncache \n\nweapon \n\n[30 seconds silence] \n\n211405 \n\n211405 \n\n211405 \n\napparatus \n\nweapon \n\ngrowth \n\n[30 seconds silence] \n\n211402 \n\n211402 \n\n211402 \n\napparatus \n\nweapon \n\ngrowth \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_XENOBACTERIA_NAME": "Xenobacteria",
        "NT_ITEM_XENOBACTERIA_PICKUP": "Damage-over-time effects may transform into a poison or blight which slows enemy attacks, but may be negated. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Alien Heads.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_XENOBACTERIA_DESC": "Inflicting a damage-over-time effect has a chance of inflicting <style=cIsHealing>poison</style>, <style=cIsVoid>blight</style>, or <style=cDeath>nothing</style> instead [<style=cIsHealing>{0}%</style>/<style=cIsVoid>{1}%</style>/<style=cDeath>{3}%</style>]. Enemies affected by poison or blight now have their <style=cIsDamage>cooldowns and attack speed reduced by {2}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{2}% per stack)</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Alien Heads.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_XENOBACTERIA_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Signal transcript ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Source from: ‘unknown’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘A location would’ve been helpful’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nWARNING \n\nWARNING \n\nDANGER OF DEATH \n\nDO NOT ENTER PORTAL \n\nVIRUS, EXTREMELY CONTAGIOUS, LETHAL \n\nINFECTED WITH NO CONTACT \n\nINFECTED THROUGH EXOSUITS \n\nDO NOT ENTER PORTAL \n\n[repeating] \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_ALTEREDSOUL_NAME": "Altered Soul",
        "NT_ITEM_ALTEREDSOUL_PICKUP": "Duplicate your on-kill effects for each kill. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Ceremonial Daggers.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_ALTEREDSOUL_DESC": "Killing an enemy drops a crystal which triggers your on-kill effects <style=cisUtility>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> <style=cisUtility>additional times.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Ceremonial Daggers.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_ALTEREDSOUL_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Audio recording transcript ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Grav receivers, Safe Travels Beta-1’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>SUBJECT-1 = Unknown, not confirmed to be UES personnel</style> \n<style=cStack>SUBJECT-2 = Unknown, not confirmed to be UES personnel</style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nSUBJECT-1 : Where have you put me? \n\nSUBJECT-2 : [unintelligible] \n\nSUBJECT-1 : Why did you imprison me here? \n\nSUBJECT-2 : [unintelligible] \n\nSUBJECT-1 : How long until I am free? \n\nSUBJECT-2 : [silence] \n\nSUBJECT-1 : Answer me. \n\nSUBJECT-2 : [silence] \n\nSUBJECT-1 : Please… \n\nSUBJECT-2 : [silence] \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_SKULLSPROUT_NAME": "Skullsprout",
        "NT_ITEM_SKULLSPROUT_PICKUP": "Collapse affects enemies randomly and reduces your cooldowns. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Brainstalks.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SKULLSPROUT_DESC": "Gain <style=cIsDamage>{0}%</style> chance to inflict <style=cIsDamage>collapse</style> on hit. <style=cIsVoid>All of your collapse effects are now transferred to a random enemy within {1}m on inflict.</style> When collapse damages an enemy, <style=cisUtility>reduce all your cooldowns by {2}</style> <style=cStack>(+{3} per stack)</style> <style=cisUtility>seconds.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Brainstalks.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SKULLSPROUT_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Fallen UES Commando’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Mira L. </style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nMaterial dating of the skull has returned a seemingly impossible result. This commando has experienced at least five thousand years in the Void. Of those years, how many did he live? \n\nThere are stalks protruding from the skull, belonging to a living parasitic plant on the inside. The bud at its base still contains traces of grey matter. The brain was likely its source of nourishment. \n\nThe stalks attach themselves to any organic matter they sense, but they only grow towards brain matter. Their favored angles of attack are through the eyes and nose. They feed on intelligence; they’ve hardly touched the beetle larvae. \n\nWhat did he experience before he died? Were his thoughts symbiotic with the sprout, or did he fade away on his own? \n\nThe sprout does not require water to survive, but seems to dry out when taken from its skull. It may be subsisting on trace amounts of the brain. There does not seem to be enough matter for this to be sustainable, and certainly not for five thousand years. \n\nOf those years, how many did he live? \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_DRENCHEDPERFORATOR_NAME": "Drenched Perforator",
        "NT_ITEM_DRENCHEDPERFORATOR_PICKUP": "Higher damage hits create increasingly devastating collapsing explosions. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Molten and Charged Perforators.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DRENCHEDPERFORATOR_DESC": "Every <style=cIsDamage>{0}% attack damage</style> dealt inflicts {1} stack <style=cStack>(+{2} per stack)</style> of <style=cIsDamage>collapse</style> on hit. On activation creates an <style=cIsVoid>explosion</style> dealing <style=cIsDamage>{3}%</style> damage in a {4}m radius, <style=cIsDamage>with each additional collapse stack inflicted increasing its radius by {5}m.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Molten and Charged Perforators.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DRENCHEDPERFORATOR_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Cavern 3.4 miles north-east of Beta-1, roughly 3 miles in’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Fragile’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Pre-analytics summary: Harvey D. </style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nA significant amount of the wildlife we found in this cave were void infected. For further reference, stand WELL clear of them as they can blink in and out of sight unexpectedly, but they can’t move too far. Especially dangerous in the dark. Cyril was bitten by one of the parasites, but it never took to him like it did the wildlife. (Needs further investigation) \n\n\Since this is for the science team’s eyes-- you’ll be happy to see this one Jade: A full, intact tooth from a void infested Magma Worm! They threw a party for Tharson after he brought back his tooth, so I better get a purple-themed void party for mine. \n\nInitial RID scans and additional recordings are attached. \n\n(To Mira: Edit this out after if you want. How have you been holding up? I wanted to message you on the company link, but we all know there’s surveillance on those. I’m getting worried. You’ve been locked in your office a lot more recently and we can’t reach you, and some are thinking that this mission’s getting too stressful for you.) \n\n(It’s okay to be stressed out. This mission is unusual, groundbreaking and completely beyond our job descriptions, and I don’t think we’ll be able to explain anything we’ve found unless we give it a decade or two... don’t put all that on yourself, alright? There are people back home who will be itching to look at these specimens.) \n\n(Some more of that lasagna you liked last time is labelled for you in the fridge.) \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_OSMIUMSHACKLES_NAME": "Osmium Shackles",
        "NT_ITEM_OSMIUMSHACKLES_PICKUP": "Slow and encumber nearby enemies, and inflict increased critical strike chance from ALL sources. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Titanic Knurls.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_OSMIUMSHACKLES_DESC": "<style=cisUtility>Weighs down</style> enemies within <style=cisUtility>{0}m</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}m per stack)</style>, slowing their movement speed, attack speed and cooldowns by <style=cisUtility>{2}%</style>, and increasing critical strike chance against them <style=cIsDamage>from ALL sources</style> by <style=cIsDamage>{3}%</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Titanic Knurls.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_OSMIUMSHACKLES_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘UES Safe Travels drop zone Alpha-2, science lab’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Mira L. </style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nThis subject has acclimated surprisingly well to the atmosphere. Within these chambers there is no open air- only oxygen-rich liquid- so a visitor must learn to drown comfortably. Instead of struggling and partially suffocating, as most would when driven by their instincts, this one knew how to breathe as soon as it awoke. \n\nThe subject is contained within the chamber and further kept still by a pair of shackles (‘stone heart’, vector 7a818e0f0f). From a 3-dimensional perspective the cuffs of these shackles seem more than wide enough for a subject to easily remove, while in Higher Reality they surround its whole body and render it immobile. The shackles appeared to be no more than crumbling metal when the subject’s team found them. \n\nThe subject has left the hysterical state noted in previous analyses and now refuses to speak or emote at all. I would like to see how it performs in a Simulacra. Something like a [???]. \n\nIt used to be so talkative, all the time. A [???] would make it talk again. \n\nI would like to hear it sing. \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_REBIRTH_NAME": "Rebirth",
        "NT_ITEM_REBIRTH_PICKUP": "The Void corrupts your inventory and grants health regeneration. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Planulae.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_REBIRTH_DESC": "Corrupts <style=cIsVoid>{0}</style> items into their <style=cIsVoid>void equivalents</style> on pickup, then corrupts <style=cIsVoid>{1}</style> items per stage. Each void item in your inventory grants <style=cIsHealing>+{2} hp/s</style> <style=cStack>(+{3} hp/s per stack)</style> of passive health regeneration. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Planulae.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_REBIRTH_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< ??? ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘「D???EEP BELOW TH?E WAV??ES】」’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Field report: The Collector </style>\n\n<style=cStack>『 Begin repo?RT ></style>\n\nI took the soft flesh of the Human in my hand.\n\nOnly 43 years of trillions touched these cells.\n\n【『UN?FOLD」」\n\nIts brain was a cross-section in time.\n\nIts potential vectors reach far beyond its dimensional cage.\n\n『EX??PAN?D』】」\n\nIt feels powerful.\n\nIt feels at home here.\n\nIt will outlive everything and everyone. It belongs here.\n\n『REBIRTH」\n\n<style=cStack>< END 」</style>",

        "NT_ITEM_TENEBRALGLAND_NAME": "Tenebral Gland",
        "NT_ITEM_TENEBRALGLAND_PICKUP": "Critical strikes cause hemmorhaging, and killing hemmorhaging enemies empowers critical strikes. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Shatterspleens.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_TENEBRALGLAND_DESC": "Gain a <style=cIsDamage>{0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style> chance to inflict <style=cDeath>hemmorhaging</style> on critical hit. Killing an enemy while they're hemmorhaging <style=cIsDamage>increases your critical strike chance and damage by {2}%</style> for {3} seconds, up to {4} times per stack. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Shatterspleens.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_TENEBRALGLAND_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Internal notes ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘???’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘???’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Written by: </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nI don’t want to sing anymore.\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_MOBIUSNODE_NAME": "Möbius Node",
        "NT_ITEM_MOBIUSNODE_PICKUP": "Regenerate shields instantly below half health. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Genesis Loops.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_MOBIUSNODE_DESC": "Gain a shield equal to <style=cIsHealing>{0}%</style> of your maximum health. Falling under <style=cIsHealth>{1}%</style> health <style=cIsHealing>regenerates all of your shields instantly</style> and stuns nearby enemies. Occurs up to {2} times <style=cStack>(+{3} per stack)</style> every {4} seconds. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Genesis Loops.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_MOBIUSNODE_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Internal notes ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style> \n\n<style=cStack>Recorded by: Mira L. </style> \n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style> \n\nThey call it the Simulacrum. \n\nGo back- remember your childhood as deeply as you can. Every moment that you can still visualize. I remember my father fishing up a massive sea bream and, after coming home with it in his hands, insisting that he’d cook it himself. Somehow, he made it taste disgusting. \n\nThen, go to your next available memory in time. I remember a school day where my shoes became untied and I fell face-first in the hallway. \n\nYou would think that these memories, and all those before and after, describe something like a linear story- the story of your life. We only see in three dimensions, and we think in four. There is a fifth, at least. \n\nIn truth, there are many vectors within Higher Reality where my father never caught a fish, and where I never left my shoe untied. All it would take is moving no more than a (micrometer?) in a Higher Reality’s space before those memories are rendered unrecognizable. Impossible, even, from the perspective of this thin slice of lower reality. Gravity and entropy only exist here, on this miniscule slice. \n\nI was shown different vectors. I saw my father as an infinite being in a fractal of feathers. I saw a world darker than the darkest black. I felt what it was like to travel from one end of the universe to another with a single step, and to enter another universe with no more than a thought. \n\nThey are not extraterrestrials. The Void isn’t their world. They watch every possible world. They have no goal or purpose but to play. Were I to stay here, I would continue to be nothing but a toy for them. I’d have to taste that disgusting fish again an infinite recurring number of times until I forgot and started again. \n\nI can’t live in this thin slice of reality anymore \n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_REBELSOUL_NAME": "Rebel Soul",
        "NT_ITEM_REBELSOUL_PICKUP": "Using your equipment grants a cloaked speed boost in which nearby enemies' life is stolen. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Little Disciples.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_REBELSOUL_DESC": "Activating your equipment grants <style=cisUtility>invisibility</style>, forcing you out of combat and increasing your movement speed by <style=cisUtility>40%</style> for <style=cisUtility>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> seconds. While invisible, <style=cIsHealing>steal {2}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{3}% per stack)</style> <style=cisHealing>hp per second</style> from non-boss enemies within <style=cisUtility>{4}m</style>. <style=cisUtility>Entering combat interrupts invisibility.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Little Disciples.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_REBELSOUL_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Field report ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘n/a’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Send directly to Captain’s office ASAP’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Field report: Harvey D. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin report ></style>\n\nSomething’s wrong. I’ve told you so many times, but you aren’t listening. Can’t you keep track of your own science team? THEY ARE IN DANGER.\n\nJade is missing. Hiram and Jules and Darren are missing. This wasn’t a routine field trip. If you looked at the reports for more than a second before you signed them off, you’d understand.\n\nWhat are you doing in your office? Sitting around waiting for more of us to be taken? LET US IN. LET US IN OR WE’LL BLAST OUR WAY IN.\n\nI won’t let you return to Safe Travels. I can smell the fuel burning and the engines of your escape ship priming. YOUR SHIP IS MORE FRAGILE THAN YOU THINK. I have something with me that will tear clean through it.\n\nWe can stop all of this if you just listen to me.\n\nCan we talk, Captain?\n\n<style=cStack>< End report ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_SPLITNUCLEUS_NAME": "Split Nucleus",
        "NT_ITEM_SPLITNUCLEUS_PICKUP": "Fully block high-damage hits. Recharge by killing elites. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Defense Nuclei.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SPLITNUCLEUS_DESC": "Fully block up to <style=cIsHealth>{0} hits</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> that damage you for <style=cIsHealth>{2}%</style> or more of your maximum health. <style=cIsDamage>Killing an elite grants {3} block charges.</style> <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Defense Nuclei.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_SPLITNUCLEUS_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Audio recording transcript ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Outside, Safe Travels drop zone Alpha-2’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘n/a’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>JD = Science team apprentice ‘Jade S.’</style>\n<style=cStack>HV = Commando designation employee ‘Harvey D.’</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nJD : You’re not serious?\n\nHV : Yeah, I really am. Point at something you want me to do the corruption thing on.\n\nJD : And it’ll turn into, like, a creepy [expletive]d up version of that thing? [laughing]\n\nHV : Just point at something!\n\nHV : Not that. [laughing]\n\nJD : Okay, what about that?\n\n[Blast of energy; likely from ‘Nullifier’ specimen]\n\nJD : What the [expletive] is that!\n\nHV : It really works.\n\nJD : I think it’s some kind of crab. A Void Crab? A ‘Vrab?’\n\nHV : We call that a ‘Vrab’, yeah.\n\nJD : That’s so awesome.\n\nHV : [laughing]\n\n[Sounds of a struggle. Note from HV: It snapped at her!]\n\nJD : [yells]\n\nHV : Oh! Did that hurt?\n\nJD : I’ll be fine. These crabs are-\n\nHV : I’ve got a first aid kit. Give me a second.\n\nJD : Thanks.\n\nHV : Maybe we shouldn’t use it like this. It was kind of a stupid idea, come to think of it. I could’ve gotten y- I could’ve gotten someone hurt.\n\nJD : [quiet laugh]\n\nHV : What?\n\nJD : I told you, I’d be fine. You’ve just given me the best research material we’ve ever had. A little scratch is nothing.\n\n[long silence]\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFROT_NAME": "Effigy of Rot",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFROT_PICKUP": "Inflict an infectious poison on melee hit which gradually heals you. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Mired Urns.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFROT_DESC": "Hitting an enemy within melee range <style=cIsHealing>poisons</style> them for {0} seconds. All of your poison or blight effects now <style=cIsHealing>heal you for {1} hp/s</style> <style=cStack>(+{2} hp/s per stack)</style> and have a <style=cIsDamage>{3}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{4}% per stack)</style> chance to <style=cIsDamage>spread to an enemy within {5}m</style> each second. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Mired Urns.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFROT_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Phsycial specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Captain’s Office’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘I’m sorry, ‘physical specimen’ was the closest category that felt applicable’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary by: Harvey D. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nWe need to understand what happened to the Captain before we can go further. I’m no doctor, but I’ll try my best.\n\nIt’s bad. We tried everything to contact him and, when he wouldn’t respond, we finally decided to cut through the blast door and barge in. When we found him, the Captain was slumped over, half on the chair and half spilled out onto the floor. The few of us who could stomach the smell stayed to write this report.\n\nAll the viscera on the floor was once his upper body and head. Where you’d expect to see blood and organs and bones is now a congealed mass of brown matter. There is heat coming from it and it’s pulsing like it has a heartbeat or maybe a breath. It has a scent like death, but sweeter.\n\nHis lower half seems mostly intact, sitting in the chair and stiff from rigor mortis. He’s so firmly seated that I can’t imagine there was any kind of struggle when he passed, so we can infer (and hope) that it was a quick death... I regret that it took us this long to know that something was wrong, but when the Captain wanted privacy, he made sure he’d have it.\n\nIf a pathogen had infected him we would all have it by now, and nothing from the science lab had been checked out by the Captain in the past two weeks. What could this be if not an attack? Given that the last appointment on his calendar was with a certain Mira L, I don’t need to use my imagination.\n\nI need to get out of here. The smell gets worse. Pungent, sweet death...\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_OBSERVERSEYE_NAME": "Observer's Optics",
        "NT_ITEM_OBSERVERSEYE_PICKUP": "Your equipment activates multiple times on a longer cooldown. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Functional Couplers.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_OBSERVERSEYE_DESC": "Your equipment activates <style=cisUtility>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> additional times on use. <style=cDeath>Multiplies equipment cooldown length by {2} for each stack</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Functional Couplers.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_OBSERVERSEYE_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Half-buried on-site at Beta-1’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Broken before I found it’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Sandra P. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nI can see everything through it. That is hardly an exaggeration: Infrared, Ultraviolet, X-Ray... and even then, sound waves, background radiation, temperature, atmospheric pressure, movement. Each lens filters all this data and more into the visible light spectrum without any electronics, with only a mechanism as simple as a small dial! With each micro-adjustment I discover a new outlook on this planet.\n\nOne unfortunate thing-- the larger lens of this object is broken in such a way that I cannot calibrate it properly. Yet, I can look into the light refracting through the shards of glass and notice subtle changes in the environment, things moving that aren’t really there, nexus points that are invisible to the naked eye but shine so brightly where the Lemurians and Beetles and other creatures tend to gather. Text that I could not understand (Think of the classic film ‘The Matrix’). I cannot imagine what else I’d see if I could only turn that main dial.\n\nThere is so much we cannot understand and it is happening all around us. I worry that, if we peer too far into the unseen, that we too will shatter.\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_APATHYCORE_NAME": "Apathy Core",
        "NT_ITEM_APATHYCORE_PICKUP": "Consumes your allies to grant shields, armor, critical strike damage and skill charges. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Empathy Cores.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_APATHYCORE_DESC": "<style=cDeath>This item will periodically consume a random allied minion</style>, granting <style=cIsHealing>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{0} per stack)</style> <style=cIsHealing>shields, {1} armor,</style> <style=cIsDamage>{2}% critical strike damage</style>, and <style=cisUtility>{3} temporary charge for all of your skills</style>. This buff is permanent or temporary <style=cStack>({4} seconds per stack)</style> based on whether the minion consumed is permanent or temporary. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Empathy Cores.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_APATHYCORE_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Audio recording transcript ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Abandoned Solus hive, 5 km from site Beta-1’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Are we sure this translation is correct?’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>SOL-1 = Abnormal Solus probe discovered at the site. Signal emitted from the probe has been translated into English for this transcript.</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nSOL-1 : KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALLKILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL\n\nSOL-1 : System storage full. Please delete unnecessary data or insert additional storage media.\n\nSOL-1 : Clearing cache...\n\nSOL-1 : KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALLKILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL KILL THEM ALL\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_DEEPVOIDSIGNAL_NAME": "Deep Void Signal",
        "NT_ITEM_DEEPVOIDSIGNAL_PICKUP": "Voidtouched enemies infest the world and cause implosions on death. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Faulty Conductors.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DEEPVOIDSIGNAL_DESC": "Activating an interactable spawns <style=cIsVoid>{0}</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style> <style=cIsVoid>Void Infestors</style> and grants <style=cisUtility>{2}</style> <style=cStack>(+{3} per stack)</style> seconds of <style=cIsVoid>Voidtouched power</style>. Voidtouched enemies now create a <style=cIsVoid>fatal implosion</style> on death. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all</style> <style=cShrine>Faulty Conductors.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DEEPVOIDSIGNAL_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Internal notes ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘N/A’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘N/A’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Recorded by: Longton R. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nIf you think the world is limited to what you can see – to what your brain can understand – you’re quite wrong. Your brain is not very powerful and can only experience a thin slice of reality at a time. It was designed with many, many limiters to prevent it from reaching any further.\n\nIf you want to know what a brain could do with a wider slice of reality, ask the denizens of the Void. They’re kind enough if you don’t shoot them on sight! When I talked to them, they wanted to show me things and give me a greater understanding of the universe, but their words meant nothing to me. Even their small-talk was too much for my human mind to grasp!\n\nWhat I did gather, though, was that there are many ways to expand the brain’s capabilities if you’re curious enough. Knowing I’d begin to go insane if I stayed too long in their presence (their words, not mine), they sent me away with a revolting little leech which they claimed could remove some of my brain’s baser limits, and a receiver with which I could listen to their lessons when I was ready.\n\nThey even gave me a few items to take back in the hopes that they would stoke my team’s curiosity. Strange that my colleagues are struggling so much with attacks-- the Void is practically running a charity!\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOP_NAME": "Proton Pop",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOP_PICKUP": "Gain {0} minutes of significantly increased speed. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Energy Drinks.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOP_DESC": "Increase your movement speed by <style=cisUtility>{0}%</style>. A stack of this item is consumed every {1} minutes. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Energy Drinks.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOP_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Alpha-1’s vending machine, for some reason’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘N/A’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>The following is printed on the label of a bottle of ‘Proton Pop!’, whose name is from an apparently nonexistent soda brand. Any errors in spelling or grammar are intentional and accurate to the label’s contents. Text transcribed by Longton R.</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nPROTON POP!\n\nThe newest Zurest Zoda pop!\n\nNow with Electrolite for FASTER ENEGY\n\nINREGIENTS: CARBONATEL WATER, HIGH!!! FRUCTORN POPUREP, CREEL, CORN, PEGGIATO ACIP, B, CARAMEL COLUOR, POP, CAFFINELLI, UNATZ\n\nALLERGY INFORTION: CONTAINS PORNED GROOSES\n\nNO ADDED POP\n\n(Note from Longton R. – Ingredients are not accurate.)\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOPCONSUMED_NAME": "Proton Pop (Consumed)",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOPCONSUMED_PICKUP": "All out of energy.",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOPCONSUMED_DESC": "All out of energy.",
        "NT_ITEM_PROTONPOPCONSUMED_LORE": "<style=cStack>No data...</style>",

        "NT_ITEM_CORALCRUST_NAME": "Coral Crust",
        "NT_ITEM_CORALCRUST_PICKUP": "Reduce damage against the first {0} hits from bosses. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Armor-Piercing Rounds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_CORALCRUST_DESC": "The first <style=cisUtility>{0}</style> hits you receive from bosses each stage have their damage reduced by <style=cisUtility>{1}%</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Armor-Piercing Rounds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_CORALCRUST_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Internal UES message thread ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘n/a’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘2058/11/01’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>LRt1 = Longton R. (UES Safe Travels, Science team)</style>\n<style=cStack>Mira Li = Mira L. (UES Safe Travels, Science team lead)</style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 17:35)</style> : As I was saying earlier, the selection of albums is really lacking. Do you think it’s something to take up with the Captain?\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 17:48)</style> : Your tastes are not something he could have predicted. I doubt the Captain has heard a polyrhythm before.\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 17:48)</style> : And what do you expect? Would you like him to compose you some more music?\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 17:50)</style> : Sure I would. Toss a couple of those trash rock albums into the Void and they’ll come back sounding good!\n(Mira Li reacted: ‘Thumbs up’)\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:05)</style> : Alright. If you have materials, I would be willing to try that.\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:06)</style> : For real?\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:06)</style> : I was mostly joking\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:07)</style> : Mostly?\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:10)</style> : I admit I’m curious what we could do by exposing mundane objects to the Void, but let’s seek approval for that first.\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:11)</style> : Approval from who? I approve the experiments taken in Alpha-1, so we need no one else’s permission.\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:11)</style> : And the Captain?\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:13)</style> : Do you trust someone with that taste in music?\n(LRt1 reacted: ‘Laughing’)\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:20)</style> : Tell me what materials you’d like.\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:21)</style> : Apparatus – Weapon – Growth. Try three items that fit those descriptors.\n\nLRt1 <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:21)</style> : Why those?\n\nMira Li <style=cStack>(2058/11/01 18:24)</style> : Bring them and I’ll tell you.\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_PREMODERNRATIONS_NAME": "Pre-Modern Rations",
        "NT_ITEM_PREMODERNRATIONS_PICKUP": "Reduce equipment cooldown and grant barrier on equipment use. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Eclipse Lites.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PREMODERNRATIONS_DESC": "Gain a <style=cIsHealing>temporary barrier</style> for <style=cIsHealing>{0} health</style> on equipment use. <style=cisUtility>Reduce equipment cooldown by {1}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Eclipse Lites.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_PREMODERNRATIONS_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘Cafeteria hall’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘Obviously not supposed to be in the cafeteria hall...’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Analytics summary: Jade S. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nLet’s get this out onto a tray.\n\nNice. What I’m seeing here is what you might expect from a military ration – there’s some kind of beef soup powder, there’s crackers, strawberry jam, canned fruits, and instant coffee. Then there are a couple extra pouches with sugar, salt, etc... I don't know if it's safe to eat but it's almost tempting.\n\nI wasn’t sure if my optics were acting up, but I spotted the year of manufacture on some of these products, and they all said 1950? These don't even look all that old, definitely not a CENTURY old, else these crackers and this jam wouldn't be recognizable as such. It still smells like strawberry! I’d hate to claim that these rations travelled through time (because everyone calls you crazy for talking about time travel), but...\n\nActually, the beef soup powder almost looks fresh. The bag it’s in must have had a perfect seal. I’ll scan it for pathogens first.\n\nIt tastes just like beef.\n\n(Note from Harvey D. – Please don’t include the part about you eating the ration. I don’t want you to get fired.)\n\n(Note from Jade S. – LOL)\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFPRIDE_NAME": "Effigy of Pride",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFPRIDE_PICKUP": "Find more boss items after using a <style=cisUtility>Shrine of the Mountain</style> or a <style=cIsVoid>Shrine of the Deep</style>. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Chance Dolls.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFPRIDE_DESC": "On use, <style=cisUtility>Shrines of the Mountain</style> and <style=cIsVoid>Shrines of the Deep</style> grant a <style=cShrine>{0}%</style> <style=cStack>(+{1}% per stack)</style> higher chance for <style=cShrine>boss item</style> drops after this stage's Teleporter event. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Chance Dolls.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_EFFIGYOFPRIDE_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Internal notes ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘void portal’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘N/A’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Recorded by: Harvey D. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nI don’t know why, but I’m feeling calm.\n\nI always hoped that my parents would see these documents and notes. I figured they’d be released to the public a little while after we were done cleaning up the remnants of the UES Contact Light, but I don’t expect any of us will be left to deliver them. We left Longton in the brig, took all the weapons and equipment we could, and marched on the nearest portal to the Void to see if we could save anyone.\n\nSome of us lost our nerve. I almost lost mine. Those who ran away are probably worm food by now, my closest colleagues are dead, and I’m hunched in a dark cave somewhere, writing my last words. I thought I’d go out screaming like a few of them did but I’m so numb that I doubt I could feel pain nor fear enough to scare me, and I expect my death to be easy like falling asleep. I’m already plenty tired.\n\nI hope that Jade had an easy death too. That seems like all I can hope for anymore. I hope it’s easy for all of us that are left.\n\nI think I know why I feel calm.\n\nI have seen so much that goes beyond my understanding that I can no longer trust my intuitions. I used to think that after death would be nothing- for an eternity, nothing- and that I would cease to experience anything. Endless, incomprehensible Void. It terrified me to think of it. But now I see that even the Void is full of strange things and that beings higher than us are treating it as their playground, and that human ideas are so absurdly small in comparison to them. Whatever happens after death, we can’t possibly understand it.\n\nIt’s better than nothing.\n\nI hear a whale call, somewhere...\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>\n<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program: No further data ></style>",

        "NT_ITEM_DREADLEECH_NAME": "Dreadleech",
        "NT_ITEM_DREADLEECH_PICKUP": "Killing enemies will heal you for each of their debuffs. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Leeching Seeds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DREADLEECH_DESC": "On kill, enemies heal you for <style=cIsHealing>{0} health</style> <style=cStack>(+{1} per stack)</style>, plus an <style=cIsHealing>additional {2} health</style> <style=cStack>(+{3} per stack)</style> for each debuff they have. <style=cIsVoid>Corrupts all Leeching Seeds.</style>",
        "NT_ITEM_DREADLEECH_LORE": "<style=cStack>< UES Contact Light Recovery Program ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Physical specimen ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Recovered from: ‘idk’ ></style>\n<style=cStack>< Comment attached: ‘???????’ ></style>\n\n<style=cStack>Pre-analytics summary: Jade S. </style>\n\n<style=cStack>< Begin transcript ></style>\n\nAbsolute mayhem in the lab today\n\nSo, you know Longton R? Science team- the one who’s been missing for weeks? He’s come back without warning and is acting odd... Odd, meaning that he tried to assault Mira and stick something in her HEAD\n\nThe thing in question is a (frankly disgusting) creature with eyes all over, something like a leech with much sharper teeth (image attached). When Longton was arrested and questioned he was apparently very relaxed about it all, and he explained that it “drains the fear from your mind” as if that’s, like, anything????\n\nI had to speak to him and he was giving me a really weird look the whole time, like a smile but a bit wonky and creepy. I asked him if he wanted anything (like water or food) and he just said “I want for nothing” with this weird grin???? Actually freaking me out to think about it and he didn’t really speak much after, I don’t want to talk to him again if that’s okay\n\n(Note from Mira L. – We cannot continue to rewrite your summaries every time. You are an adult, use professional language and proper punctuation.)\n\n<style=cStack>< End transcript ></style>"
    }
}